      "message": "Nit: would it be OK to drop this include? `p3s_4k_unsupported()` already reaches `net/ipv4/tcp.c` through `\u003clinux/mm_types.h\u003e`, which includes `\u003clinux/p3s.h\u003e` at its end, and the merged refusals (e.g. `io_uring/memmap.c`, `kernel/bpf/syscall.c`, `drivers/vfio/vfio_main.c`) don\u0027t include it either. I checked that it still builds without the include in the 16k-p3s, 4k-native, 16k-nop3s and x86_64 configs.\n\nThen `tcp.c` would only carry the hook, and upstream changes to its include list couldn\u0027t conflict with it.",
